Subject: read unit_amount when price is missing

The vendor's 2026-10-01 version stopped sending `price` and now returns the value in a new `unit_amount` field (the published spec still lists only `price`), so `get_product` read `p.price`, got undefined, and emitted `price: null`, violating the notNull contract. The fix falls back to `unit_amount` when `price` is absent (`p.price ?? p.unit_amount ?? null`), which keeps the v1 fixture—where `price` is present—producing identical output while correctly pricing the new version.

